"News0Body" = "In this sample story, the house lights slowly fade and the first note breaks the silence. Blue light moves across the stage as every instrument adds to the evening’s story. The visuals seem to take part in the performance rather than simply accompany it.\n\nThis article was written for Mizon’s news design preview. It does not report a real concert. Imagine following photos, performance stories and updates from your favorite artists here in the future.";
"News0Category" = "On stage";
"News0Summary" = "A visual story of the moments before a show, where light, sound and the audience’s anticipation meet.";
"News0Title" = "The night the stage comes alive";
"News1Body" = "Hours of rehearsal and coordination lie behind this imagined performance. The sound crew checks instruments, lighting follows the rhythm and musicians review final changes. The audience has not arrived yet, but the show is already taking shape.\n\nThis sample article demonstrates the news section. It looks at details the audience rarely sees. From the first rehearsal to the final applause, every moment has a story worth hearing.";
"News1Category" = "Backstage";
"News1Summary" = "The details behind a live show: setting the stage, rehearsing as a band and preparing for the opening moment.";
"News1Title" = "From the first rehearsal to the final applause";
"News2Body" = "This imagined music video follows a short journey through the city at night. Street lights, camera movement and the main character’s pauses follow the rise and fall of the music. Every frame reveals a little of the story without explaining everything in words.\n\nThis is a design sample, not a report about a released work. Its idea is to show stories that connect music and cinema and invite the audience to discover something new.";
"News2Category" = "Music video";
"News2Summary" = "City lights, cinematic frames and a compact story make the visuals an extension of the music.";
"News2Title" = "When a music video becomes a short film";
"News3Body" = "This sample story imagines a brief pause: a window facing the rain, a quiet piano and a few minutes away from the rush of the day. The tracks in this scene have space to breathe. The silence between notes matters as much as the melody.\n\nThis text was written to preview the news section and does not introduce a real collection. Stories like this could sit alongside release updates and listening suggestions, making music discovery a calm, personal experience.";
"News3Category" = "Listening experience";
"News3Summary" = "Rain and gentle melodies offer space to discover music that gives a busy day room to breathe.";
"News3Title" = "A quieter wave: sounds for a pause";
